# Chromium/Chrome user-data profile written into the repository root.
# NOT produced by AEGIS: the only --user-data-dir in this repo is
# bench/lib/sensor.js:261, which points at os.tmpdir() (see profileDirFor).
# A Chrome 151 profile landed here on 2026-08-15 from an external launch flag
# — a browser started with --user-data-dir set to the clone root. Browser
# profile data is not ours to publish, so keep a recurrence untracked and
# visible as ignored rather than one `git add -A` away from a public commit.
# Every rule is root-anchored: a bare `Default/` or `Variations` would also
# swallow a same-named directory anywhere under src/ or tests/.
/ActorSafetyLists/
/AmountExtractionHeuristicRegexes/
/BrowserMetrics/
/CaptchaProviders/
/CertificateRevocation/
/component_crx_cache/
/Crashpad/
/Crowd Deny/
/Default/
/extensions_crx_cache/
/FileTypePolicies/
/FirstPartySetsPreloaded/
/GPUPersistentCache/
/GrShaderCache/
/hyphen-data/
/MEIPreload/
/OnDeviceHeadSuggestModel/
/optimization_guide_model_store/
/OptimizationHints/
/OriginTrials/
/PKIMetadata/
/PrivacySandboxAttestationsPreloaded/
/RecoveryImproved/
/Safe Browsing/
/SafetyTips/
/segmentation_platform/
/ShaderCache/
/SSLErrorAssistant/
/Subresource Filter/
/TrustTokenKeyCommitments/
/WasmTtsEngine/
/WidevineCdm/
/ZxcvbnData/
# These four land as plain files, not directories — no trailing slash, or the
# rule silently matches nothing (`Variations` is Chrome's seed file).
/first_party_sets.db*
/Last Browser
/Last Version
/Local State
/Variations
